  "scope": "Private captured-provider Store custody, protected host liveness/ownership restrictions, actual public Service/native source binding and HTTP projection with controlled provider receipts, and captured-call validation in existing public/private HTTP/WS jobs. The live typed observation pipeline and worker action integration remain unfinished.",
  "observations": [
    "Private source construction requires the original private purpose/context and committed exact provider acknowledgment. It derives the original Connection, generation, Participant, correlation and pair audience. Uncommitted/wrong receipts and a foreign retained reader are refused. Ordinary read/context credentials do not grant publication.",
    "Current private memory validation is shared with private media forwarding. Every original listener retains current history authorization, current private lifetime and captured incarnation. Provider closure, uncertain export, generation change and a revoked human listener history grant hide buffered derived content and refuse late publication. Continued AI access does not lend that human authority.",
    "Private media readers include the complete current Conversation identity interval needed by observation projection. Protected private publication and page reads reuse that original proof before a queued writer; generic publication refuses contention. The writer completes after the original reader drops, with no fallback authority upgrade.",
    "Routes can retain a protected SessionObservationActivity restriction. Busy errors propagate instead of advancing a cursor over temporarily unavailable data. Explicit closure hides sensitive content synchronously without requiring cleanup SQL. A different activity or generic binding cannot replace an existing restriction under the same correlation. Failed registration does not insert a route before SQL success.",
    "Service factories bind the exact actual native registry entry/generation and captured public/private provider memory. Their owned source closes on explicit close/drop. The Store retains only its restriction, not ownership. Runtime stop/missing registry entries remove access; ambiguous adapter/registry contention preserves cursors. Activity checks do not perform Store callbacks, authority waits or IO inside SQL.",
    "The actual runtime probe uses a signed registered native Connection, Service public source factory/publication and public HTTP observation reads. It verifies attribution and both explicit close/owner drop before Store provider cleanup, while current provider/native metadata and Service memory reads remain independently valid. Its provider receipts are controlled Store fixtures: this probe does not claim actual provider creation/export or live event decoding.",
    "The bounded shared decoder now validates captured call assertions before public initial/update ACKs, public monitor/audio terminal events, private ACK/final transcript/terminal events and cleanup terminal reports. The existing actual native/HTTP/WS journey adds foreign update ACK and foreign terminal cases; neither confirms update delivery nor marks the owned call ended. Cleanup still targets the original captured call, with logical replay sending no creation/export again.",
    "Protocol observation and HTTP wire shapes remain unchanged. No upstream patch, persistent schema, compatibility layer, downgrade or external publication was added. All source handling remains data-only; requests/results do not execute handoffs."
  ],
